// WHY: generic type parameters (`<T>`) on functions, types, and enums.
// Parsing lives in parser.av (extends Parser with parse_type_params).
// Declaration parsers (fn_decl, struct_decl, enum_decl) call
// parse_type_params when they see `<` after the declaration name.
// The monomorphization pass (mono.av) consumes List<TypeParamEntry> to generate
// concrete specializations before codegen.
//
// dir-as-module (g2eo.1): no `mod` decls — sibling .av files
// (parser.av + mono.av) auto-load and surface flat at
// `features.generics.{...}`.
